 Integrating Argo CD with GitHub
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure Argo CD on a Linux machine
Connect Argo CD to a GitHub repository for GitOps workflows
Deploy a sample application from a GitHub repository using Argo CD
Understand the GitOps deployment model and its benefits
Monitor and manage application deployments through the Argo CD web interface
Troubleshoot common integration issues between Argo CD and GitHub
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with Git and GitHub operations
Basic knowledge of YAML file structure
Understanding of containerized applications
Experience with Linux command line operations
A GitHub account (free account is sufficient)
